package components

// LLMRequired is the ONE setup notice for a surface whose feature needs a model.
//
// WHY IN A SHARED LEAF. A feature that needs an LLM (review, chat, and any
// recipe that asks the model something) must be able to say so without
// importing the feature that happened to write the sentence first. Recipes may
// not import each other (cmd/check-flatdeps enforces it), and this package is
// the trim-proof layer every page layout already calls into — the same reason
// ActionResult lives here.
//
// WHY NOT A BOOLEAN. `LLMRequired(configured bool)` would make one component
// render either a notice or nothing, which hides the branch from the caller. The
// caller already knows whether it has a model; it renders the notice in the
// branch that lacks one and the real UI in the other. One sentence, one source,
// the decision where the knowledge is.
//
// The sentence names the knob, because "LLM not configured" without the fix is
// the kind of error that costs a support round trip.
templ LLMRequired(surface string) {
	<div class="alert alert-warning" role="status">
		<span>{ surface } needs a configured LLM. Set GOAI_API_KEY on the server, then reload.</span>
	</div>
}
